1
00:00:08,940 --> 00:00:13,360
Brighten up the peace,
then step away and see.

2
00:00:24,220 --> 00:00:27,020
Hello, goodbye.

3
00:00:27,020 --> 00:00:31,500
The one who finishes their
business and goes right home.

4
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:35,360
Wappara-puwa, wappara.

5
00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:39,920
Wa-wa-wa-wa-wa-wa.

6
00:00:40,900 --> 00:00:45,540
Don't panic, in this narrow town.

7
00:00:45,540 --> 00:00:49,380
Where are you going? Haste makes waste.

8
00:00:49,920 --> 00:00:54,700
What if there's someone even better

9
00:00:54,700 --> 00:00:58,540
than me?

10
00:00:59,370 --> 00:01:02,960
Tell me, tell me all night long.

11
00:01:08,460 --> 00:01:12,800
I don't mind waiting.

12
00:01:12,800 --> 00:01:17,000
Because I'm a Kameza woman.

13
00:01:17,920 --> 00:01:21,740
I won't lose, I'm a Ginza woman.

14
00:01:21,740 --> 00:01:26,520
I'll love you for years and years.

15
00:01:27,140 --> 00:01:29,980
This is the way of the Kameza woman.

16
00:01:36,220 --> 00:01:37,480
Idiot!

17
00:01:38,020 --> 00:01:40,440
What is this?
Betting on horse races during work hours!

18
00:01:40,440 --> 00:01:41,644
No, well, that's just...

19
00:01:41,694 --> 00:01:45,040
I only have fifteen thousand yen left
for this month's living expenses, so...

20
00:01:45,040 --> 00:01:48,100
I thought I'd use that as
capital and hit it big in one go.

21
00:01:48,100 --> 00:01:50,940
Come on, Ryo-chan, you just got your pay!

22
00:01:50,940 --> 00:01:52,860
What did you spend it on, senpai?

23
00:01:52,860 --> 00:01:57,080
Well, what else? This month's main attraction,
Dream Station 3, of course!

24
00:01:57,080 --> 00:02:00,620
Plus software too:
Bio Inferno and Brigitte Nielsen Ch...

25
00:02:00,620 --> 00:02:02,400
And the limited-edition
Blackboard model kit.

26
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:04,420
Ojingar Z and Great Ojingar.

27
00:02:04,420 --> 00:02:05,700
And I bought figures too.

28
00:02:05,700 --> 00:02:07,420
Bibilman and Bibilman Lady.

29
00:02:07,420 --> 00:02:08,620
And that Brabra thing.

30
00:02:09,860 --> 00:02:11,640
What a shortsighted guy you are.

31
00:02:11,640 --> 00:02:13,820
If you keep pouring your
money into that kind of stuff,

32
00:02:13,820 --> 00:02:16,120
your living expenses will be gone in no time,
you know.

33
00:02:16,120 --> 00:02:17,760
I'm trying to win that back,

34
00:02:17,760 --> 00:02:19,000
and I want the Mouse one too.

35
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:21,300
You can't make money with that kind of thing,
obviously.

36
00:02:21,300 --> 00:02:23,260
Think more realistically.

37
00:02:23,260 --> 00:02:25,040
Well, that's just how he is.

38
00:02:25,040 --> 00:02:26,320
There's no such thing, no way.

39
00:02:26,800 --> 00:02:27,740
Pouring good money in...

40
00:02:27,740 --> 00:02:31,020
It's money earned through
such a sloppy work attitude,

41
00:02:31,020 --> 00:02:33,700
so of course you spend it so carelessly.

42
00:02:33,700 --> 00:02:38,060
Now is the time to mend your
ways and start working seriously.

43
00:02:38,060 --> 00:02:42,380
Money earned through sweat
and toil is truly valuable.

44
00:02:42,380 --> 00:02:46,360
But whether you earn it through
hard work or make a quick profit,

45
00:02:46,360 --> 00:02:48,140
money is still money, isn't it?

46
00:02:48,140 --> 00:02:50,580
Then wouldn't it be better
to make it the easy way?

47
00:02:50,580 --> 00:02:51,660
Idiot!

48
00:02:52,120 --> 00:02:55,700
Change that foolish thinking,
or your pay gets docked starting next month!

49
00:02:55,700 --> 00:02:56,020
Hey!

50
00:02:56,460 --> 00:03:00,100
In the end, those who work diligently
and steadily are the ones who win.

51
00:03:00,100 --> 00:03:05,100
Anyone who doesn't understand that is a
fool who doesn't know the true joy of living.

52
00:03:05,580 --> 00:03:07,640
Well, I'm heading back
to the main station now.

53
00:03:07,640 --> 00:03:08,360
Yes, sir!

54
00:03:08,360 --> 00:03:09,180
Thank you for your hard work.

55
00:03:12,240 --> 00:03:15,451
Ryo-san,

56
00:03:15,501 --> 00:03:18,220
are you in?

57
00:03:19,180 --> 00:03:20,980
Y-yes, in the back room.

58
00:03:20,980 --> 00:03:21,780
What's wrong?

59
00:03:22,020 --> 00:03:23,620
Suke-san, help me!

60
00:03:23,620 --> 00:03:24,500
Just come here.

61
00:03:26,860 --> 00:03:27,580
Matsukichi.

62
00:03:30,040 --> 00:03:31,120
Who the heck is that?

63
00:03:31,120 --> 00:03:32,580
I knew it, you're lying!

64
00:03:32,580 --> 00:03:34,240
You know Ryo-san?

65
00:03:34,240 --> 00:03:37,620
That's cold, Ryo-san!
It's Matsukichi, Matsukichi Kato.

66
00:03:37,620 --> 00:03:38,820
Matsukichi Kato.

67
00:03:38,820 --> 00:03:42,000
Remember? Ten years ago, last winter, at
the convenience store in front of the station.

68
00:03:42,720 --> 00:03:45,500
Ten years ago,
the convenience store at the station.

69
00:03:55,140 --> 00:03:56,300
This is heavy, you know.

70
00:03:57,220 --> 00:03:57,540
This is...

71
00:03:59,140 --> 00:04:01,040
You were trying to shoplift, weren't you?

72
00:04:02,740 --> 00:04:04,120
It's cops like you

73
00:04:04,120 --> 00:04:06,180
who are reading porn magazines on duty.
Is that really okay?

74
00:04:07,340 --> 00:04:07,900
This is

75
00:04:10,260 --> 00:04:12,080
I was in the middle of a stakeout.

76
00:04:12,080 --> 00:04:14,720
Because of you, I lost sight of the star!

77
00:04:15,500 --> 00:04:16,420
A stakeout

78
00:04:19,720 --> 00:04:21,960
You're that shoplifting
bastard from back then!

79
00:04:21,960 --> 00:04:22,940
Long time no see, man.

80
00:04:22,940 --> 00:04:24,380
What do you want?

81
00:04:25,540 --> 00:04:27,300
Ryo-san, about this one...

82
00:04:27,300 --> 00:04:29,440
To Ryotsu Kankichi

83
00:04:29,440 --> 00:04:32,100
Suit, 15,000 yen total.

84
00:04:32,540 --> 00:04:33,260
What is this?

85
00:04:34,080 --> 00:04:36,720
When he tried it on, he tore the clothes.

86
00:04:36,720 --> 00:04:39,060
On top of that, he says he has no money.

87
00:04:39,560 --> 00:04:41,220
So he said since he knows Ryo-san,

88
00:04:41,220 --> 00:04:43,340
to just bill Ryo-san.

89
00:04:43,800 --> 00:04:44,420
Thanks.

90
00:04:45,500 --> 00:04:48,480
Don't joke! I don't have any money either!

91
00:04:48,620 --> 00:04:50,320
I'm not lending you any money!

92
00:04:50,660 --> 00:04:51,800
Reigo! Reigo!

93
00:04:52,360 --> 00:04:52,620
You don't have any?

94
00:04:52,680 --> 00:04:54,420
Just sew up the torn part for me!

95
00:04:54,460 --> 00:04:55,860
Come on, hurry up and sew it!

96
00:04:58,040 --> 00:05:00,300
There's no way I'm returning it now!

97
00:05:00,380 --> 00:05:01,820
No matter what, you're paying for it!

98
00:05:02,040 --> 00:05:03,540
Ryo-san, please!

99
00:05:03,880 --> 00:05:05,560
Hey! Don't cling to me!

100
00:05:05,620 --> 00:05:06,960
Let go of me, I said!

101
00:05:07,100 --> 00:05:09,800
These guys don't have any money to lend you!

102
00:05:09,920 --> 00:05:11,920
What? My wallet?

103
00:05:41,800 --> 00:05:43,320
Sounds like days of overflowing freedom

104
00:05:44,220 --> 00:05:46,120
Unemployed, then. Address?

105
00:05:46,500 --> 00:05:47,260
Address

106
00:05:47,600 --> 00:05:49,720
Well, going wherever the wind
blows and wherever the mood takes me,

107
00:05:49,740 --> 00:05:52,280
I'd say I'm a free-spirited drifter,
I guess.

108
00:05:52,580 --> 00:05:53,940
No fixed address, then.

109
00:05:54,180 --> 00:05:55,240
Guarantor?

110
00:06:01,240 --> 00:06:05,200
I'm asking if you have any relatives
who'd pay back fifteen thousand yen to me.

111
00:06:05,560 --> 00:06:07,100
Leave the money matters to me.

112
00:06:07,100 --> 00:06:08,428
Well, for the starting capital, yeah,

113
00:06:08,478 --> 00:06:11,235
if you could lend me about
a hundred thousand yen,

114
00:06:11,285 --> 00:06:13,920
I'll have it doubled and paid back by tomorrow,
I promise.

115
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:15,020
How?

116
00:06:15,540 --> 00:06:18,206
Well, just between us, see,

117
00:06:18,256 --> 00:06:21,360
you just put two or three races
into the gaps of a sure thing.

118
00:06:21,620 --> 00:06:23,851
Then, as a bonus, it's not just double,

119
00:06:23,901 --> 00:06:25,780
I'll pay it back triple.

120
00:06:29,140 --> 00:06:32,940
Idiot! If it were that easy,
I'd be a horse racing millionaire by now!

121
00:06:33,680 --> 00:06:34,720
Then 50,000 yen is fine.

122
00:06:35,180 --> 00:06:36,820
What kind of logic is that?

123
00:06:36,820 --> 00:06:38,900
Those two are alike, aren't they?

124
00:06:38,900 --> 00:06:41,340
They're just as irresponsible as each other.

125
00:06:41,340 --> 00:06:43,000
Then no more talk about horse racing.

126
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:46,700
Instead,
there's a way to make big money easily.

127
00:06:47,600 --> 00:06:48,360
Can't say.

128
00:06:48,360 --> 00:06:51,960
It's quietly been expanding its
reach at festival food stalls.

129
00:06:51,960 --> 00:06:53,200
Chocolate banana

130
00:06:53,200 --> 00:06:54,240
Banana

131
00:06:54,240 --> 00:06:56,640
It stirred up a whirlwind in
the Japanese sweets industry.

132
00:06:56,640 --> 00:06:58,120
Strawberry daifuku

133
00:06:58,120 --> 00:06:59,220
So what?

134
00:06:59,220 --> 00:07:02,480
That's why I came up with the third
installment of the big-hit fruit series.

135
00:07:02,480 --> 00:07:03,620
Miso melon

136
00:07:04,720 --> 00:07:08,120
Hey, with this, a huge hit is guaranteed.
We'll rake in the money.

137
00:07:08,380 --> 00:07:12,360
Wow, I'm a genius.
My own sense is starting to scare me.

138
00:07:12,680 --> 00:07:14,734
Who's going to eat this total dud?

139
00:07:14,784 --> 00:07:17,000
It's not like you can just stick things together,
you know.

140
00:07:17,360 --> 00:07:20,760
Then, how about Manju Yon Shimai,
to rival Dango Sanshimai?

141
00:07:21,380 --> 00:07:23,680
How about Chibi-Maru-Bon, to rival Sazaebon?

142
00:07:24,360 --> 00:07:25,980
To rival the Nelton Party,

143
00:07:26,040 --> 00:07:28,320
I never have to rival anyone
for the rest of my life!

144
00:07:28,720 --> 00:07:31,434
Sure, but making money easily is only
for one in tens of thousands of people,

145
00:07:31,484 --> 00:07:33,620
those with outstanding luck and talent.

146
00:07:34,720 --> 00:07:38,800
If you think an ordinary guy like you can make money with an idea that small,
you're dead wrong.

147
00:07:39,280 --> 00:07:42,400
Listen, Matsukichi,
think more realistically.

148
00:07:42,400 --> 00:07:45,900
It's time to turn over a new leaf
and think about working honestly.

149
00:07:45,900 --> 00:07:50,200
Listen, money earned through sweat and
toil is the only money with real value.

150
00:07:51,720 --> 00:07:55,040
In the end, people who have diligently
worked away at things are the ones who win.

151
00:07:55,880 --> 00:08:00,280
Anyone who doesn't understand that is a great
fool who doesn't know the true joy of living.

152
00:08:00,280 --> 00:08:02,920
You've grown quite a bit.

153
00:08:06,300 --> 00:08:16,980
Grumbling, as if I've heard that line somewhere before...
Now that I think about it, what you said, Chief, is absolutely right.

154
00:08:16,980 --> 00:08:23,920
I'm deeply reflecting on it, and I find myself
hoping he won't make the same mistake I did.

155
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:28,700
Well, at least he seems to
be pretending to reflect.

156
00:08:28,700 --> 00:08:31,340
So the manuscript is cancelled too, then.

157
00:08:31,340 --> 00:08:33,480
That depends on your attitude from now on.

158
00:08:33,480 --> 00:08:36,180
Ryotsu Kankichi,
I'll be allowed to apply myself to my work.

159
00:08:36,700 --> 00:08:38,400
Here, it's fixed now.

160
00:08:38,400 --> 00:08:40,180
Thank you very much, Suke-san.

161
00:08:41,320 --> 00:08:44,340
I see. Borrowing money from Ryotsu,
you must be really desperate.

162
00:08:44,340 --> 00:08:45,800
What do you mean?

163
00:08:46,240 --> 00:08:48,240
If you're looking for a
place where he can work,

164
00:08:48,240 --> 00:08:50,140
I have one lead in mind, too.

165
00:08:50,140 --> 00:08:52,280
Lend me money instead of that job, please.

166
00:08:52,280 --> 00:08:54,600
No, no, I'll take him there right away, yes.

167
00:08:56,700 --> 00:08:59,220
We've been having trouble,
we're short on delivery staff.

168
00:08:59,220 --> 00:09:01,400
You can start with us today if you like.

169
00:09:01,400 --> 00:09:02,260
That's great.

170
00:09:02,260 --> 00:09:03,600
Matsukichi, it's settled!

171
00:09:03,600 --> 00:09:06,820
Hey, a young, cute girl like you

172
00:09:06,820 --> 00:09:09,400
why would you be working at a stingy,
filthy shop like this?

173
00:09:10,140 --> 00:09:11,380
What time do you get off today?

174
00:09:11,380 --> 00:09:13,160
Want to go grab something good to eat?

175
00:09:13,720 --> 00:09:14,760
That's enough already!

176
00:09:14,760 --> 00:09:16,340
It's this young lady, I mean.

177
00:09:16,340 --> 00:09:17,240
Come over here.

178
00:09:17,240 --> 00:09:22,640
You bastard,
you blew the introduction to Chief Ohara!

179
00:09:24,600 --> 00:09:25,200
Which one are you going with?

180
00:09:25,600 --> 00:09:28,420
If I'm gonna work anyway, something in a cool building,
like a foreign company, would be nice.

181
00:09:29,020 --> 00:09:30,680
Plus I'd just ruin my suit.

182
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:34,340
What foreign company
would hire a punk like you?

183
00:09:34,980 --> 00:09:36,380
Then how about becoming an artist?

184
00:09:36,540 --> 00:09:37,880
I'm really good at karaoke, you know.

185
00:09:38,020 --> 00:09:40,220
I'll make a promo tape and go pitch myself,
I'm telling you.

186
00:09:41,120 --> 00:09:43,180
I wonder if Ryo-chan and the
others are doing all right?

187
00:09:43,580 --> 00:09:46,465
If Ryotsu keeps looking
after the young ones like that,

188
00:09:46,515 --> 00:09:47,920
he'll grow on his own.

189
00:09:48,120 --> 00:09:50,240
Look at others' ways and correct your own.

190
00:09:53,480 --> 00:09:55,400
Hey, what do you really want?

191
00:09:55,960 --> 00:09:58,480
Anything that's easy and pays well,
I don't care.

192
00:09:58,880 --> 00:10:01,480
If there were something like that,
I'd already be doing it myself.

193
00:10:02,160 --> 00:10:04,220
Give it a little serious thought,
for crying out loud.

194
00:10:04,700 --> 00:10:07,480
Enough. I'm getting my money back no matter what,
mark my words.

195
00:10:15,900 --> 00:10:17,340
That actually suits you

196
00:10:18,040 --> 00:10:19,940
Senpai, that's Matsukichi-san's, isn't it?

197
00:10:20,120 --> 00:10:22,060
I'm holding onto it as
collateral for a debt.

198
00:10:22,060 --> 00:10:24,680
So what kind of job have
you had Matsukichi-san doing?

199
00:10:24,940 --> 00:10:26,500
W-well, that's...

200
00:10:27,940 --> 00:10:30,180
Yes, this is Kameari Kōen-mae Police Box.

201
00:10:30,180 --> 00:10:31,240
What?!

202
00:10:33,600 --> 00:10:37,200
That spineless coward! He went and
abandoned the job I finally found for him!

203
00:10:37,500 --> 00:10:39,180
This time he's not getting off free!

204
00:10:40,860 --> 00:10:42,160
It's a letter addressed to Matsukichi.

205
00:10:42,580 --> 00:10:43,580
Chiyo Kato.

206
00:10:44,140 --> 00:10:45,620
No, not good, Ryo-chan!

207
00:10:47,340 --> 00:10:47,760
Shut up!

208
00:10:47,760 --> 00:10:51,640
In that case, he's a fugitive
who skipped out on his debts.

209
00:10:51,640 --> 00:10:54,860
This is official business, strictly official,
to track down his whereabouts.

210
00:10:56,460 --> 00:10:57,460
To Big Brother,

211
00:10:57,900 --> 00:11:00,860
You haven't written in ages.
Are you doing well?

212
00:11:01,480 --> 00:11:05,200
Dad is actually going to be hospitalized for an illness,
it looks like.

213
00:11:05,620 --> 00:11:07,060
He won't say it out loud, but

214
00:11:07,060 --> 00:11:09,740
Dad really wants to see you, Big Brother.

215
00:11:10,200 --> 00:11:13,040
Mom says you don't have to
make a fuss or put on airs.

216
00:11:13,040 --> 00:11:15,760
She always says she wants
you to come home soon.

217
00:11:17,400 --> 00:11:19,000
Please come home soon.

218
00:11:22,280 --> 00:11:22,680
Hey.

219
00:11:23,760 --> 00:11:27,640
You're not planning to rob a bank or something,
are you?

220
00:11:32,680 --> 00:11:34,980
The one planning that is my little sister.

221
00:11:36,140 --> 00:11:39,360
Ten years ago, I had a huge fight with Dad.

222
00:11:42,720 --> 00:11:45,160
I'm never going to end up like Dad,
you hear?

223
00:11:45,780 --> 00:11:48,900
What's this bastard criminal
got to talk back to me for?

224
00:11:49,400 --> 00:11:50,500
See ya, Mom.

225
00:11:50,500 --> 00:11:51,160
Let's do it.

226
00:11:51,880 --> 00:11:52,520
Matsukichi

227
00:11:52,520 --> 00:11:53,460
Big brother

228
00:11:58,800 --> 00:12:01,140
I told my sister I'm a young businessman.

229
00:12:01,860 --> 00:12:03,380
Having boasted big when I left,

230
00:12:03,380 --> 00:12:05,120
I can't go back until I've hit it big.

231
00:12:05,120 --> 00:12:06,800
I'd be too embarrassed to go back.

232
00:12:06,800 --> 00:12:08,480
So what about your big score?

233
00:12:08,480 --> 00:12:10,380
Miso melon, or a bank robbery?

234
00:12:11,140 --> 00:12:12,480
Don't put on airs in front of your family.

235
00:12:12,480 --> 00:12:14,540
I'll cover your train fare somehow.

236
00:12:15,160 --> 00:12:16,480
Just go back to the countryside
without saying anything.

237
00:12:18,140 --> 00:12:19,520
Besides, depending on the folk song,

238
00:12:19,520 --> 00:12:21,820
you could pass for a young businessman.

239
00:12:22,560 --> 00:12:24,360
These days, young businessmen

240
00:12:24,360 --> 00:12:27,020
often have more debt than assets, you know.

241
00:12:27,480 --> 00:12:28,420
Compared to that,

242
00:12:28,420 --> 00:12:30,180
you're much richer than they are.

243
00:12:30,820 --> 00:12:31,480
Ryo-san,

244
00:12:33,220 --> 00:12:35,060
I'm going back after ten years.

245
00:12:35,060 --> 00:12:36,580
Isn't it bad to show up empty-handed?

246
00:12:36,800 --> 00:12:38,260
As a young businessman,

247
00:12:40,180 --> 00:12:41,200
Uncle Sakata and

248
00:12:41,200 --> 00:12:43,060
Auntie Hashiguchi gets the small one

249
00:12:43,640 --> 00:12:46,040
Goro, Akio, and the triplets,
it's gotta be sake, right?

250
00:12:47,240 --> 00:12:48,760
I shouldn't have said anything.

251
00:12:49,340 --> 00:12:50,920
Excuse me, 30 of these, please.

252
00:12:50,920 --> 00:12:53,080
You're planning to buy souvenirs
for everyone in the village?

253
00:12:53,640 --> 00:12:55,560
Mom loves these, too.

254
00:12:55,560 --> 00:12:57,700
Buying Hakata mentaiko as a Tokyo souvenir

255
00:13:00,020 --> 00:13:01,060
Well then, take care.

256
00:13:01,060 --> 00:13:02,760
Thanks for everything, Ryo-san.

257
00:13:03,360 --> 00:13:06,820
Once things settle down over there, you pay back
the money you borrowed from me first, got it?

258
00:13:12,640 --> 00:13:16,040
Matsukichi, let go, the doors are closing!
Hey, let go!

259
00:13:16,080 --> 00:13:16,340
Right!

260
00:13:20,480 --> 00:13:23,520
Sorry, I just got carried away.

261
00:13:23,600 --> 00:13:25,020
Do I look like your girlfriend?!

262
00:13:25,740 --> 00:13:28,400
Since it's come to this, let's just
go all the way to Morioka together.

263
00:13:28,820 --> 00:13:32,620
Why would I go all the way to Morioka? I'm turning back at the next station,
I tell you.

264
00:13:32,760 --> 00:13:34,360
Omiya, Omiya.

265
00:13:35,460 --> 00:13:37,040
You're really a handful.

266
00:13:37,540 --> 00:13:37,860
Well then.

267
00:13:39,100 --> 00:13:40,160
Like I'd fall for that.

268
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:46,200
I just don't have the guts to go home alone.

269
00:13:46,200 --> 00:13:48,020
What are you talking about?
Hurry up and get back on.

270
00:13:48,020 --> 00:13:50,460
I don't know what face I'm
supposed to go home with.

271
00:13:51,120 --> 00:13:53,380
That face is fine.
Go like that, just as you are.

272
00:13:53,380 --> 00:14:03,040
Our country fish is really good, you know.

273
00:14:06,700 --> 00:14:08,220
Yes, one ticket to Morioka.

274
00:14:08,740 --> 00:14:09,860
Was it a wrongful transfer of a suspect?

275
00:14:09,860 --> 00:14:12,560
No, he's a habitual small-time swindler.

276
00:14:12,660 --> 00:14:14,140
Thank you for your hard work.

277
00:14:14,480 --> 00:14:15,800
Come on, Ryo-san.

278
00:14:15,980 --> 00:14:19,880
Hehe, but a young businessman and a cop together,
that's totally legit, right?

279
00:14:22,900 --> 00:14:25,940
Wow, you've really changed.

280
00:14:28,220 --> 00:14:29,840
That suit suits you, Ryo-san.

281
00:14:30,420 --> 00:14:33,060
Let's get our story straight
so you're my secretary.

282
00:14:33,780 --> 00:14:36,060
And you're paying me back for this suit too.

283
00:14:36,860 --> 00:14:38,480
Hey, how much longer until we get there?

284
00:14:40,340 --> 00:14:43,660
Two and a half hours?
There's a reason for that, you know.

285
00:14:43,660 --> 00:14:44,740
Should we turn back?

286
00:14:44,740 --> 00:14:47,900
The closer we get,
the more nervous I'm getting.

287
00:14:47,900 --> 00:14:49,600
After coming all this way,
you're saying that?

288
00:14:49,600 --> 00:14:52,120
Alright, then let's do a rehearsal.

289
00:14:52,120 --> 00:14:52,880
Rehearsal?

290
00:14:55,080 --> 00:14:55,900
Ready?

291
00:14:56,400 --> 00:14:56,800
Yes.

292
00:14:56,800 --> 00:14:59,360
Okay, then, start!

293
00:14:59,360 --> 00:14:59,740
Yes.

294
00:15:00,740 --> 00:15:02,860
I-I-I'm home!

295
00:15:03,340 --> 00:15:06,300
Wrong! When you get home,
you open the door first.

296
00:15:06,300 --> 00:15:07,060
Yes.

297
00:15:07,060 --> 00:15:10,180
Okay, *rattle rattle*, I'm home.

298
00:15:11,780 --> 00:15:14,330
Uh...

299
00:15:14,380 --> 00:15:18,280
How's the old man doing?

300
00:15:18,400 --> 00:15:21,660
Idiot, how could a sick man be doing well?

301
00:15:21,660 --> 00:15:23,660
Right...

302
00:15:23,660 --> 00:15:25,980
Say something else, something different.

303
00:15:25,980 --> 00:15:26,380
Yes.

304
00:15:26,380 --> 00:15:27,400
Good luck.

305
00:15:27,400 --> 00:15:30,920
Hey, Dad, you're not dead yet?

306
00:15:30,920 --> 00:15:33,740
Idiot, what are you doing
picking a fight with a sick man?

307
00:15:34,920 --> 00:15:36,440
You look pretty healthy, after all.

308
00:15:37,060 --> 00:15:38,300
Say it with a bit of embarrassment, like,

309
00:15:38,300 --> 00:15:40,460
that's the usual pattern for
this kind of situation, right?

310
00:15:40,880 --> 00:15:41,720
Yeah, I suppose.

311
00:15:41,720 --> 00:15:42,900
Alright, I'm counting on you.

312
00:15:42,900 --> 00:15:45,640
Dad, you look pretty healthy!

313
00:15:45,640 --> 00:15:49,080
I-I-I haven't been beaten yet, you know!

314
00:15:49,080 --> 00:15:51,000
What are you saying?

315
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:54,120
Why would you say something that
excites a sick man like that?

316
00:15:54,940 --> 00:15:56,120
What do you want me to say to that?

317
00:15:58,020 --> 00:15:58,820
The scent of the sea.

318
00:16:00,240 --> 00:16:00,920
Whoa.

319
00:16:17,660 --> 00:16:19,760
Dad, ever since I left home,

320
00:16:19,760 --> 00:16:21,880
he's apparently been
working at this fish market.

321
00:16:22,500 --> 00:16:24,560
Don't you want to become a fisherman?

322
00:16:24,560 --> 00:16:27,460
Me? The mornings are early
and the work is brutal.

323
00:16:27,460 --> 00:16:28,460
No way, I'm not joking.

324
00:16:28,460 --> 00:16:31,380
Besides, I'm going back to Tokyo again.

325
00:16:32,060 --> 00:16:34,360
Matsukichi! It's Matsukichi!

326
00:16:35,200 --> 00:16:37,480
I heard you've been getting ahead in Tokyo.

327
00:16:37,480 --> 00:16:38,900
It's nothing that grand.

328
00:16:39,980 --> 00:16:43,680
It's a cheap little thing, but it's a souvenir from Tokyo,
so please share it with everyone.

329
00:16:44,940 --> 00:16:45,660
Thanks a lot.

330
00:16:46,020 --> 00:16:49,700
Speaking of which, your dad hasn't been around since yesterday.
Did something happen?

331
00:16:58,900 --> 00:16:59,640
Figures.

332
00:16:59,640 --> 00:17:00,240
Hey.

333
00:17:03,560 --> 00:17:04,300
Aaaaah.

334
00:17:05,820 --> 00:17:13,780
Sorry, nobody's home... Hello! I thought the voice sounded familiar, and it's Matsukichi!
I wondered whose dad that was, and it's Goro.

335
00:17:14,620 --> 00:17:19,920
Here's a souvenir. By the way, nobody's home.
Do you know where they went?

336
00:17:19,920 --> 00:17:26,780
You don't know? Your dad was admitted to the hospital.
Chiyo and your mom are at the hospital too, both admitted.

337
00:17:43,420 --> 00:17:44,440
Big brother

338
00:17:44,440 --> 00:17:45,440
Matsukichi

339
00:17:45,440 --> 00:17:47,080
Mom, Chiyo

340
00:17:50,060 --> 00:17:50,840
Dad

341
00:17:50,840 --> 00:17:51,960
Matsukichi

342
00:17:51,960 --> 00:17:52,820
Big brother

343
00:17:52,820 --> 00:17:54,740
Pull yourself together, Matsukichi!

344
00:17:54,740 --> 00:17:55,780
You're the eldest son, aren't you?

345
00:17:57,400 --> 00:17:58,880
It's okay, it's okay.

346
00:17:59,480 --> 00:18:01,560
That stubborn old man isn't going to die.

347
00:18:06,380 --> 00:18:09,260
Doctor, is Dad all right?
Was the surgery a success?

348
00:18:09,720 --> 00:18:11,680
Yes, it was a success.

349
00:18:12,700 --> 00:18:13,580
Thank you, Doctor.

350
00:18:14,780 --> 00:18:17,140
Well, then, thank you.

351
00:18:18,740 --> 00:18:19,480
Dad.

352
00:18:20,360 --> 00:18:21,040
Dad!

353
00:18:22,160 --> 00:18:23,700
Pull yourself together, Dad!

354
00:18:23,700 --> 00:18:26,140
It's me, your son Matchi!

355
00:18:27,120 --> 00:18:30,000
I'm back, I'm back, Dad!

356
00:18:32,440 --> 00:18:35,500
You idiot, don't shout like that,
it's embarrassing!

357
00:18:37,140 --> 00:18:38,180
Excuse me.

358
00:18:40,360 --> 00:18:42,920
For someone who just had major surgery,
you're awfully lively.

359
00:18:42,920 --> 00:18:45,500
Sorry, about Dad's illness...

360
00:18:45,500 --> 00:18:46,740
It's hemorrhoids.

361
00:18:46,740 --> 00:18:47,060
Hemorrhoids?

362
00:18:49,260 --> 00:18:51,420
Matsukichi, by the way, who's this?

363
00:18:51,620 --> 00:18:53,520
This is Ryotsu-kun, my secretary.

364
00:18:53,520 --> 00:18:53,920
Nice to meet you.

365
00:18:53,920 --> 00:18:54,780
Hello.

366
00:18:56,780 --> 00:18:58,640
Who the hell invited this idiot?

367
00:18:59,120 --> 00:19:01,100
I didn't want to come, either!

368
00:19:01,100 --> 00:19:04,600
Now, now, you two.
It's not like you're kids fighting.

369
00:19:04,600 --> 00:19:07,460
Dad, come on,
don't turn your back like that.

370
00:19:07,460 --> 00:19:08,520
This way is more comfortable.

371
00:19:08,880 --> 00:19:12,140
You're embarrassed.
You really wanted to see him, didn't you?

372
00:19:12,140 --> 00:19:13,480
Who'd want to see him?

373
00:19:14,180 --> 00:19:16,460
Uncle said to do it just like we rehearsed.

374
00:19:16,460 --> 00:19:19,300
But that man was a G, you know.

375
00:19:19,300 --> 00:19:20,640
Start from the G, then.

376
00:19:20,640 --> 00:19:21,360
Okay.

377
00:19:23,620 --> 00:19:26,600
Anyway, Dad seems to be doing well.
That's good.

378
00:19:27,220 --> 00:19:32,380
Well, that's hardly true. His good-for-nothing son wore him out,
and that's why he got worse, isn't it?

379
00:19:32,380 --> 00:19:32,920
What was that?

380
00:19:32,920 --> 00:19:36,980
Dad, he came all this way to see us.
You don't have to talk to him like that.

381
00:19:36,980 --> 00:19:38,480
Yeah, it's been ten years!

382
00:19:38,480 --> 00:19:43,220
Ten years without showing your face, and
you turn up looking all flashy like that!

383
00:19:43,720 --> 00:19:45,980
Where exactly do you think I look flashy?

384
00:19:45,980 --> 00:19:48,000
You do, so I'm saying you do.

385
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:48,440
What did you say?

386
00:19:49,140 --> 00:19:49,780
Dad.

387
00:19:50,560 --> 00:19:51,920
Calm down, Matsukichi.

388
00:19:52,880 --> 00:19:53,740
Got it.

389
00:19:54,500 --> 00:19:56,080
What are you talking about, Dad?

390
00:19:56,780 --> 00:20:02,680
I'm doing great. Even today I
squeezed over here between busy jobs.

391
00:20:03,160 --> 00:20:12,500
I've always been quick to catch trends, ever since I was over there.
I make clothes and I've been a huge success in the apparel industry. The company's grown fast, recession or no recession.

392
00:20:12,880 --> 00:20:22,820
A building in prime Meguro Aoyama? And we're opening overseas branches soon! Wow,
really? Mr. Ryotsu?

393
00:20:22,820 --> 00:20:24,260
Yeah, well.

394
00:20:24,260 --> 00:20:26,600
Here, a souvenir.

395
00:20:26,600 --> 00:20:28,580
This is a Hermès scarf.

396
00:20:29,480 --> 00:20:30,820
Thanks, big brother.

397
00:20:30,820 --> 00:20:31,500
Here, a bag.

398
00:20:31,500 --> 00:20:33,780
Hakata mentaiko.

399
00:20:34,280 --> 00:20:36,000
I managed to talk to
Dad with plenty of energy.

400
00:20:36,480 --> 00:20:37,640
Putting on airs, aren't you.

401
00:20:37,640 --> 00:20:38,980
I'm not putting on airs.

402
00:20:38,980 --> 00:20:41,120
I told you, I'm not like Dad.

403
00:20:41,120 --> 00:20:43,380
I'll never end up like Dad.

404
00:20:43,380 --> 00:20:44,440
Like that guy.

405
00:20:44,440 --> 00:20:46,840
I'm not the type of man who'll spend
his whole life in a place like this.

406
00:20:49,100 --> 00:20:52,400
Look at the time already.

407
00:20:53,220 --> 00:20:56,340
I have a meeting today,
so I have to get back by evening, right?

408
00:20:56,800 --> 00:20:58,020
Hey, Ryotsu.

409
00:20:59,640 --> 00:21:01,940
Chiyo, give this to
the neighbors or someone.

410
00:21:01,940 --> 00:21:03,540
Big brother, are you leaving already?

411
00:21:04,700 --> 00:21:06,280
Being the president is tough.

412
00:21:06,900 --> 00:21:07,900
Well then, take care.

413
00:21:07,900 --> 00:21:11,180
President,
I'll handle today's meeting on your behalf.

414
00:21:11,180 --> 00:21:13,900
Please stay here with them a little longer,
President.

415
00:21:15,200 --> 00:21:17,140
No, that's not really possible.

416
00:21:17,140 --> 00:21:17,640
But...

417
00:21:17,640 --> 00:21:19,280
Speak up, Ryotsu.

418
00:21:23,040 --> 00:21:24,940
Ryotsu-kun, what are you doing?

419
00:21:24,940 --> 00:21:26,860
My Armani cost a lot, you know.

420
00:21:26,860 --> 00:21:29,180
Sorry, I'm just a bit of a brute.

421
00:21:29,180 --> 00:21:31,300
I have a meeting, and that's a problem.

422
00:21:32,280 --> 00:21:33,500
That's enough, Matsukichi.

423
00:21:34,220 --> 00:21:36,120
Don't you dare put on any more airs.

424
00:21:37,520 --> 00:21:38,240
Dad.

425
00:21:38,620 --> 00:21:39,800
Even if you stay here with us...

426
00:21:39,800 --> 00:21:42,740
I hear about you through rumors on the wind.

427
00:21:43,360 --> 00:21:46,020
At your age, you can't even
afford a proper set meal, can you?

428
00:21:46,020 --> 00:21:48,500
Putting on airs and pretending to
be a company president like that.

429
00:21:48,500 --> 00:21:50,640
It's painful just to listen to.

430
00:21:55,160 --> 00:21:55,800
Matsukichi.

431
00:21:55,800 --> 00:21:56,520
Matsukichi.

432
00:21:56,520 --> 00:21:57,240
Mr. Ryochi.

433
00:21:57,820 --> 00:22:01,440
My foolish son has been a bother to you.

434
00:22:02,080 --> 00:22:03,680
No, I, that is...

435
00:22:03,680 --> 00:22:06,200
It was my upbringing that was at fault.

436
00:22:06,200 --> 00:22:09,240
He turned out to be a spoiled,
good-for-nothing half-wit.

437
00:22:09,740 --> 00:22:12,160
But his life belongs to him.

438
00:22:12,160 --> 00:22:15,620
I think he should just
live however he likes.

439
00:22:16,860 --> 00:22:17,900
However he likes.

440
00:22:29,800 --> 00:22:31,100
Sorry to keep you waiting.

441
00:22:31,620 --> 00:22:34,920
So what's it going to be, Matsukichi?
Are you going back to Tokyo after all?

442
00:22:36,120 --> 00:22:37,740
These are the local specialties here.

443
00:22:37,740 --> 00:22:39,220
Take some with you as a souvenir.

444
00:22:40,480 --> 00:22:42,280
So you're staying, then?

445
00:22:43,780 --> 00:22:46,040
Dad's really become an old man, hasn't he.

446
00:22:47,900 --> 00:22:49,860
I figured it couldn't be
helped if you didn't know.

447
00:22:50,340 --> 00:22:52,580
Honestly, Dad, you're such a troublemaker.

448
00:22:58,220 --> 00:22:59,660
Yoisa!

449
00:23:00,040 --> 00:23:00,820
He's come to!

450
00:23:01,060 --> 00:23:02,120
You've never seen anything like it,
have you!

451
00:23:02,360 --> 00:23:04,180
Let go! Let go!

452
00:23:04,360 --> 00:23:06,620
People are watching!
They'll get the wrong idea!

453
00:23:06,800 --> 00:23:08,440
Come on! Let go!

454
00:23:11,560 --> 00:23:13,780
This is Matsukichi-kun?

455
00:23:14,060 --> 00:23:15,940
You've become quite the burly man.

456
00:23:17,920 --> 00:23:20,600
Ryo-san,
thank you for looking after me back then.

457
00:23:21,120 --> 00:23:24,307
I wanted to pay back the money
I borrowed with my first paycheck,

458
00:23:24,357 --> 00:23:26,100
but we ended up drinking
it all with everyone.

459
00:23:26,660 --> 00:23:29,800
In its place, though it may not be much,
I'm sending you a huge amount of butter.

460
00:23:30,420 --> 00:23:32,880
I'm really going to become
a fisherman this time.

461
00:23:33,420 --> 00:23:35,884
Dad keeps saying I'll never stick with it,

462
00:23:35,934 --> 00:23:38,220
so I told him I'll keep
at it no matter what.

463
00:23:38,900 --> 00:23:41,203
I'm planning a fishing boat
experience tour right now,

464
00:23:41,253 --> 00:23:43,360
so please come along and
have fun with everyone.

465
00:23:43,940 --> 00:23:49,640
Set sail before sunrise, experience fishing until you can't stand for a whole day,
and eat all the fish you want.

466
00:23:50,080 --> 00:23:54,220
It solves the labour shortage and cuts labour costs,
two birds with one stone, pure profit!

467
00:23:54,680 --> 00:23:56,000
What do you think of this idea?

468
00:23:56,400 --> 00:23:57,740
I don't think it's cool.

469
00:24:43,360 --> 00:24:45,420
Something irreplaceable,

470
00:24:45,420 --> 00:24:50,880
how much of it can a person
ever hold in a lifetime?

471
00:24:52,660 --> 00:24:57,240
You are me, and I am you.

472
00:24:58,340 --> 00:25:02,300
That alone was enough to fulfil me.

473
00:25:03,180 --> 00:25:08,460
Just seeing you smile,

474
00:25:08,460 --> 00:25:15,040
I felt as if every hardship had been healed.

475
00:25:42,320 --> 00:25:43,720
Thanks for watching.

